OS 4.0
variable served  ok
: serve ( conn -- ) begin pad 256 2 pick get-line dup 0< 0= while pad swap 2 pick send-line repeat drop close-connection  1 served +! ;  ok
: line-server ( -- ) 5000 listen begin 5000 accept-connection ['] serve spawn drop again ;  ok
task server  ' line-server server start  ok
: settled? ( -- flag ) conns @ 0= served @ 32 = and ;  ok
: settle ( -- ) 110000 deadline begin 200 ms settled? over expired? or until drop ;  ok
settle served @ .  conns @ count-list . 32 0  ok
create fake-conn /conn allot  fake-conn /conn 0 fill  ok
fake-conn 0 0 0 2000 ' segment-out catch . 2drop 2drop drop -24  ok
\ A connection freed after MY-IP changed still leaves its hash bucket (defect 31)  ok
new-conn constant c1  ip 10.0.2.2 c1 c.rip !  1234 c1 c.rport !  5000 c1 c.lport !  c1 hash-in  ok
my-ip @  ip 10.0.2.99 my-ip !  c1 free-conn  my-ip !  c1 conn-bucket @ c1 = . 0  ok
\ CLOSE-CONNECTION waits while another task holds CONNS-LOCK across pauses, as the sweep does, then frees once  ok
task sweeper  : hold ( -- ) conns-lock get  20 0 do pause loop  conns-lock release ;  ok
new-conn constant c2  ' hold sweeper start  pause  c2 close-connection  free-conns @ c2 =  c2 c.link @ c2 <> and . -1  ok
1000 ms  ok
